ithout knowing the exact PRD filename, I can't list it correctly in required_reading since the field spec requires actual file paths, not directories. I'm checking the project context for clues—I see references to orphaned PRDs like prd012 and prd013, and prd011 for magefiles, but I need to find which PRD corresponds to this task. Looking at the implementation_status in ARCHITECTURE.yaml might give me the version information I need to identify the right file.\n\nNow I'm noticing a discrepancy in the roadmap and implementation_status—several commands like wc, sponge, and cat are marked as \"spec complete\" with rel01.1 versions, but the roadmap shows rel01.1 is specifically for \"Batch 1.1 -- cat specification and differential test.\" I need to reconcile whether these other commands should actually be at different release versions or if the roadmap is incomplete.\n\nFor now, I'll focus on the current task which is rel01.1 for cat. Since I don't have the actual file listing, I'll reference the use case file I know exists (rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml) and note that it should point to the PRD file, or I can suggest looking in the product-requirements directory for the cat PRD. I'm setting up the required_reading to be actionable by having the agent start with the use case file, which contains a reference to the PRD it needs to read, then also including the architecture and module files for context. I'm considering whether to add the test suite file, but deciding it's probably not necessary for the implementation task since testing is separate. I need to implement the cat utility with four core requirements: reading files in order and outputting to stdout, handling stdin when no files are given or \"-\" is passed, supporting the key flags like -n for line numbering and -b for non-blank numbering plus -s for squeezing blank lines, and properly handling errors with appropriate exit codes and stderr messages.\n\nMy approach is to keep everything in a single main.go file under cmd/cat/ without subpackages, avoid importing test utilities into production code, and stick strictly to what the PRD specifies rather than adding extra GNU cat features. The acceptance criteria cover building successfully, concatenating multiple files in order, reading from stdin when needed, and implementing the required flags correctly. I'm verifying the task structure is complete and well-formed—all sections are present with the right number of items. The main challenge is that I don't know the exact PRD filename, but I can work around that by having the stitch agent read the use case first to locate the PRD. For the task title, I'll use \"prd-cat\" as a shorthand since I can't include the specific PRD number without knowing it upfront.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15840,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15840},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2de1ffe0-46e8-40d6-900f-1ba24ef14e54","uuid":"c940a1a2-e154-42b9-90b5-4f6cbb9496ab"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01EwMunj2eQZPq5H3ycApDUr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nAll information is in the provided `project_context` field. No file reads needed.\n\n## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem solved**: Formal specifications are derived from C source code for classic Unix utilities, which are then used to generate verified Go implementations via an AI code generation pipeline. Behavioral parity is confirmed through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `docs/` — human-authored PRDs, use cases, test suites (read by pipeline, never written by it)\n- `cmd/<utility>/` — Go implementation + differential tests per utility\n- `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/format/`, `pkg/testutils/` — shared library for syscalls, formatting, and differential harness\n- `magefiles/` — Mage build targets; boundary between human-guided spec phase and automated synthesis\n- Four-stage pipeline: extract → specify (human) → synthesize (orchestrator) → verify (differential tests)\n\n**Current state**:\n- Code exists at `generation-merged` tags for `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/ts`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`\n- No generated code on the current working branch (`generation-gh-262-codegen`, clean)\n- `cmd/ls` and `cmd/du` have complete specs but no code generation yet\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease scope is restricted to **[01.1]** per the constraint. The roadmap entry:\n\n```\nversion: \"01.1\"\nname: Batch 1.1 -- cat specification and differential test\nspecstatus: spec_complete\nusecases:\n  - id: rel01.1-uc001-cat\n    specstatus: spec_complete\n    codestatus: not started\n```\n\nThe spec is complete (PRD + use case + test suite exist). Code generation has not run on this branch. Per canonical ordering (P8), the implementation task precedes the test task. With a 1-task limit, the implementation task is proposed first.\n\n**Dependencies**: `go.mod` and `pkg/` packages (sys, testutils) are already scaffolded or at generation-merged tags. `cmd/cat/main.go` has no blocking code dependency.\n\n## Step 4: Task Proposal\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/cat prd-cat R1-R4 -- implement core concatenation\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml (read first; contains the cat PRD filename -- locate and read that PRD from docs/specs/product-requirements/ before implementing)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure, pkg/sys and pkg/format descriptions, generation scope exclusions in design decision 7)\n      - go.mod (module path and Go version)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: cat utility -- concatenate files and write to stdout\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Read each file argument in order and write its contents verbatim to stdout, per the cat PRD R1\n      - id: R2\n        text: When no file arguments are given or an argument equals \"-\", read from stdin and write to stdout, per the cat PRD R2\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement all flags listed in the cat PRD, including at minimum -n (number all output lines), -b (number non-blank output lines only), and -s (collapse consecutive blank lines to one blank line)\n      - id: R4\n        text: Exit 0 on success; exit non-zero and write a diagnostic message to stderr when any file cannot be opened or read, per the cat PRD exit code contract\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: cmd/cat/main.go is the only production source file for this task; do not create sub-packages within cmd/cat/\n      - id: D2\n        text: Do not import pkg/testutils in main.go -- that package is for test files only\n      - id: D3\n        text: Derive all flag behavior and edge cases from the cat PRD; if a flag is not in the PRD, do not implement it\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/cat/ completes with no compiler errors or warnings\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Running the binary with one or more file arguments writes the concatenated contents of those files to stdout in argument order\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Running the binary with no arguments or with \"-\" as an argument reads from stdin and writes to stdout\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"-n numbers every output line; -b numbers only non-blank lines; -s collapses consecutive blank lines into a single blank line\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: The binary exits 0 when all inputs are processed successfully; exits non-zero and prints an error to stderr when any file cannot be opened or read\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15840,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15840},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2de1ffe0-46e8-40d6-900f-1ba24ef14e54","uuid":"ac85d472-6673-4146-a2bb-54814ea8d4f9"}
